From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:05:02 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Invalidation: keep translations across permission
 flips, revive unchanged blocks, fixed code buffer

Three switches, all default off (behaviour identical to the previous commit without them):
- MACRUNNER_FEX_PROT_KEEP=1: a protection change of already-executable memory to executable
  without write access no longer throws the translation away; =2 additionally arms a write
  trap on whole host pages when the range becomes RWX. Plan in Common/MacRunnerProtKeep.h.
- MACRUNNER_FEX_REVIVE=1: a block invalidated while its guest bytes are unchanged is returned
  to service by XXH3 hash instead of being recompiled (same block map, same buffer epoch,
  executable range, no TF, same Mono mode; classes in Core/MacRunnerRevive.h).
- MACRUNNER_FEX_CODEBUF_MAX=1: start with the maximal code buffer (128 MiB) so growth does not
  flush every translation (upstream does this for its code cache).
Counters callret_clears/callret_ms measure the call-ret stack clearing cost.
Elden Ring runs showed 33-40 % repeated compilations and ~12.3k invalidations (~45 GB) per run.
Host tests: 200k random plans and 20k random page maps, with failing mutants as negative controls.
Not measured in a game yet.

